.SH BUGS
.B -t
drives the rules, the mount, the buying and the unmount, and reads the
pixels back to check the climber is drawn on both sides of the wrap.
It presses no key: the tables that turn a key into an action are covered
by nothing and have only ever been checked by playing.
.PP
A room served from another machine is untested.
Nothing here would have to change for it \- a room is mounted, and a
mount does not care where the other end is \- but the claim that has
been demonstrated is a room in another process, not a room on another
host.
.PP
A room may keep a read waiting for ever and the game will wait with it:
there is no timeout on any of the four files, and a slow or wedged room
wedges the climb.
.PP
Nothing checks that the tower can be climbed.
The map is data and can be edited into a tower with a gap too wide to
jump.
